From: halt95 <halt95@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 19:06:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 53/76] v2 teardown: reserve the shared counter before
 unlinking PLE shm names (Astra P1); balanced-lifetime subprocess test (Astra
 P2)

Astra review of 3a407727ab (record flashnext-v2-teardown-fix-astra-r1-2026-09-14): after our
manual unlink, RefcountedMapAllocator::close() still calls shm_unlink when a storage's shared
counter reaches zero and raises on ENOENT - a C++ exception in a destructor, so a worker could
abort at storage destruction (TP!=0 input buffers are not process-lifetime pinned). Reproduced:
the round-2 balanced tests against the 3a407727ab connector abort the test process
("Fatal Python error: Aborted", testlogs/shmfix-r2-red-on-3a407727ab.log).

connector.py: _unlink_filename_shared_storage() now takes a per-connector reserved-filename set,
calls storage._shared_incref() once per backing name before os.unlink (kept on success or ENOENT;
rolled back with _shared_decref() on any other OSError; an incref failure returns without
unlinking); repeated close()/release_host_storage() cannot reserve twice; the guessed torch
helper-name probe is removed. Shutdown ordering, CUDA registrations and tensor references are
unchanged; one reservation per backing allocation is deliberately left until process exit.

tests/v1/ple_offload/test_shm_unlink.py: fixtures balance ForkingPickler dumps with loads;
new test_close_balanced_filename_storage_lifetime_exits_cleanly runs the real close() ordering
in a subprocess, drops every reference, collects, requires exit 0 and a repeated release;
reservation-once and rollback tests on a fake storage (rollback assertion corrected by Fable:
aliases retry a rolled-back name within one pass, so increfs == decrefs, nothing reserved).
Green 12/12 focused; full tests/v1/ple_offload 138 passed / 1 skipped.
Sol draft (sol-shm-fix-r2), Fable applied/tested.
